# Maps, geocoding and address autofill
OpenStreetMapMenuMap=Map
OpenStreetMapMapOfThirdparties=Map of third parties
OpenStreetMapMapOfContacts=Map of contacts
OpenStreetMapMapOfMembers=Map of members
OpenStreetMapCountGeo=%s records: %s on the map, %s could not be located, %s not geocoded yet.
OpenStreetMapNominatimSlow=Addresses outside the Netherlands are located with Nominatim, at most 1 per second, so this may take a while. You can keep working in other pages meanwhile. Results are stored, each address is searched only once.
OpenStreetMapFollowingAddressCantBeLocalized=These addresses could not be located:
OpenStreetMapGeocoding=Geocoding and autofill
OpenStreetMapGeocodingDesc=Addresses in the Netherlands are located with the PDOK Locatieserver (Dutch government, BAG data, free, no key). Other countries use Nominatim (OpenStreetMap). No Google service is used. Coordinates are stored and searched again only when the address changes.
OpenStreetMapPdokAutofill=Fill street and town from postcode and house number (Netherlands)
OpenStreetMapPdokAutofillDesc=Adds a house number field next to the zip code on third party, contact and member forms. The request is done by your Dolibarr server.
OpenStreetMapNominatimEmail=Contact email for Nominatim
OpenStreetMapNominatimEmailDesc=Recommended by the Nominatim usage policy, so the operators can contact you in case of problems.
OpenStreetMapNominatimUrl=URL of Nominatim search service
OpenStreetMapTileUrl=URL of map tiles
OpenStreetMapTileAttribution=Map attribution (HTML)
OpenStreetMapEmptyForDefault=Keep empty to use the default value.
OpenStreetMapErrorUrlMustBeHttps=Value of %s must start with https://
OpenStreetMapCache=Stored coordinates
OpenStreetMapCacheDesc=%s addresses are stored with their coordinates.
OpenStreetMapClearCache=Clear stored coordinates
OpenStreetMapCacheCleared=Stored coordinates cleared
OpenStreetMapEuAutofill=Address suggestions for all countries
OpenStreetMapEuAutofillDesc=Suggestions while typing the address (street, house number, postcode and town), with Photon on OpenStreetMap data, free. Outside the Netherlands also the town from the postcode (dictionary of Dolibarr, then Nominatim). The requests are done by your Dolibarr server and cached.
OpenStreetMapPhotonUrl=URL of Photon search service
OpenStreetMapMenuMapContacts=Show the entry "Map" also in the menu of contacts
OpenStreetMapMenuMapContactsDesc=Only useful when contacts have their own address. The map pictogram on the card of a contact does not depend on this option.
OpenStreetMapGeocodingInProgress=Locating the other addresses, one by one...
OpenStreetMapStopGeocoding=Stop
OpenStreetMapGeocodingDone=All addresses have been searched.
OpenStreetMapGeocodingStopped=Stopped. The other addresses will be searched on a next visit.
OpenStreetMapGeocodingServiceUnavailable=The geocoding service does not answer. The other addresses will be searched on a next visit.
OpenStreetMapQualityTitle=What to expect in each country:
OpenStreetMapQualityOSM=Outside the Netherlands, addresses come from OpenStreetMap, free and open. How complete they are depends on the country: good in most of Western Europe, while house numbers or postcodes may be missing in some countries (for example Greece and parts of Eastern Europe). Then only the street is suggested and you type the number yourself.
OpenStreetMapQualityFairUse=The public servers of Photon and Nominatim are free for fair use and without guarantee. Answers are stored, so each address is asked only once. With many users, enter the URL of your own server below.
OpenStreetMapQualityNL=In the Netherlands, PDOK (Dutch government, BAG) is used when enabled: complete and up to date.
OpenStreetMapQualityDictionary=Towns of postcodes can also come from the dictionary of zip codes and towns of Dolibarr, which you can complete in the tab "Zip codes and towns".
OpenStreetMapQualityPaid=For better addresses in some countries, a paid service can be used with your own key (Postcode.eu, see below).
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEu=Postcode.eu (optional, paid, own key)
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuDesc=For the selected countries, the address suggestions come from the international address API of Postcode.eu instead of OpenStreetMap. A subscription and a key of Postcode.eu are needed; each search is billed by Postcode.eu. Answers of this service are not stored by the module.
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuPrivacy=The addresses typed by your users are sent to Postcode.eu. Check that you have a data processing agreement with this provider (GDPR).
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuKey=API key
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuSecret=API secret
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuSecretSet=Stored (keep empty to keep it)
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuCountries=Countries using Postcode.eu
OpenStreetMapPostcodeEuCountriesDesc=Other countries keep the free service.
OpenStreetMapZiptown=Zip codes and towns
OpenStreetMapZiptownDesc=Dolibarr has its own dictionary of zip codes and towns. When it knows a postcode, this module takes the town from it, without asking an external service. Here you can complete it for a country with the free list of GeoNames, or with your own file. Only missing zip codes and towns are added; existing ones are never changed.
OpenStreetMapZiptownUseDictionary=Use the dictionary for the autocompletion of zip codes and towns of Dolibarr
OpenStreetMapZiptownUseDictionaryDesc=Option of Dolibarr itself (MAIN_USE_ZIPTOWN_DICTIONNARY). This module uses the dictionary in any case.
OpenStreetMapZiptownImport=Complete the dictionary
OpenStreetMapZiptownSourceGeonames=Download the list of GeoNames for this country
OpenStreetMapZiptownSourceFile=Upload a file
OpenStreetMapZiptownFileFormat=File of GeoNames (zip or txt), or a text file with one zip code and town per line, separated by a tab, a semicolon or a comma. UTF-8.
OpenStreetMapZiptownImportButton=Import
OpenStreetMapZiptownImported=%s zip codes and towns added, %s already present.
OpenStreetMapZiptownDownloadFailed=The list of GeoNames could not be downloaded. Download it yourself and upload the file.
OpenStreetMapZiptownBadFile=No zip code and town found in this file for this country.
OpenStreetMapZiptownFileTooLarge=The file is too large.
OpenStreetMapZiptownContentTooLarge=The content of this file is too large (more than 30 MB). For Great Britain, use GB.zip (postcode districts, for example AL3) instead of GB_full: the town of a full postcode is then found with its first part.
OpenStreetMapZiptownMaxSize=Max size of a file on this server: %s.
OpenStreetMapZiptownGazetteer=This file is the GeoNames gazetteer (all geographical names, without postal codes). Use the postal codes file instead: https://download.geonames.org/export/zip/ (same country code, for example GR.zip).
OpenStreetMapZiptownGeonamesLicense=Data of GeoNames (www.geonames.org) is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License.
OpenStreetMapZiptownContent=Content of the dictionary
